course: dictionary
lesson: 11564
title: Ancestry: your family line
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your ancestry is all the people in your family who lived long before you, such as great-grandparents and the people before them. It also means the places and groups those people came from. «She is of Irish ancestry» tells you that her family came from Ireland, long ago.
explain: Clue words help you. The sentence «Ella traced her ancestry back to a village in Italy» uses traced, which means followed step by step. So to trace your ancestry is to find out, one family step at a time, who your ancestors were and where they lived.
explain: An ancestor is one person in your ancestry, like your great-grandmother. Ancestry is the whole line of them, all the way back. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Our family's ancestry is a long list of farmers» only makes sense if ancestry means the family line.
fact: Your ancestry is all the people in your family who lived long before you.
fact: Ancestry can also mean the places or groups your family came from, as in «of Irish ancestry».
fact: An ancestor is one person in your ancestry, such as a great-grandparent.
fact: Family-history projects often use a family tree to show your ancestry.
fact: Ancestry has a plural too: ancestries, meaning several different family lines.
exercise: «Maya traced her ancestry back to a village in Italy.» What does ancestry mean here? | *All the people in her family who lived long before her, and where they came from | Her favourite food from the village market | A holiday she took last summer
exercise: «Her ancestors built the old mill by the river.» Find and copy one word that means a person from your family who lived long before you. | river | old | *ancestors | built
exercise: «Sam is of Irish ancestry.» What does this tell you? | He can dance an Irish jig | *His family came from Ireland, long ago | He has lots of Irish friends at school
test: «Our class made family trees to explore our ancestry.» What is the best meaning of ancestry? | *The people in our family who lived long before us, and where they came from | Games we play at break time | Pets we keep at home
test: Which of these is an ancestor? | Your best friend from school | A cousin who lives next door | *Your great-grandmother, who lived long before you were born
exam: Lina says, «My ancestry is the holiday I took in Spain.» What does ancestry really mean? | *The family who lived long before her, and where they came from | The name of her hotel | Her favourite place in Spain | Her plans for next year's holiday
